  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the exact solution to $4\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)+4\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)=8.$",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithms share the same base, and so we can combine them using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)+4\\operatorname{log}⁡(x) & =8 \\\\ 4[\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)+\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)] & =8 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x) & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(5x) & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(5x) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)} & ={10}^{2} \\\\ 5x & =100 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
